Original commit body from a39cf66:

When the sketch runs static analysis, it now computes an estimated test
coverage by counting how many non-test functions/methods are directly
called by test code. This replaces the generic "Coverage requires
execution" message with something like "~35% estimated coverage
(460/1318 functions called by tests)".

Key changes:
- Add _estimate_test_coverage() to compute coverage from call graph
- Modify _run_analysis() to compute coverage BEFORE filtering test files
- Update _format_test_summary() to accept optional coverage_stats
- Update generate_sketch() to pass coverage stats to test summary

This is a static approximation based on direct call edges. It doesn't
track transitive calls or runtime-only coverage, but gives users a
useful signal about test coverage without requiring test execution.
